01:17:19.560 --> 01:17:22.540
Do you want to know where and how?

877
01:17:22.540 --> 01:17:33.220
In the in the sacrament of the Holy Eucharist, in it the sacrifice is continuous, the pressure

878
01:17:33.220 --> 01:17:39.900
is perpetual that I put on the Father to use mercy on creatures and on souls in whom to

879
01:17:39.900 --> 01:17:42.020
obtain their love.

880
01:17:42.020 --> 01:17:46.780
So he puts pressure on the Father to obtain mercy for creatures and he puts pressure on

881
01:17:46.780 --> 01:17:49.820
souls to obtain our love.

882
01:17:49.820 --> 01:17:54.340
And he says, I find myself in a continuous contrast dying continuously, but they're all

883
01:17:54.340 --> 01:17:56.260
deaths of love.

884
01:17:56.260 --> 01:18:01.660
So what he's saying to Louisa here is that she has been asked from the very beginning

885
01:18:01.660 --> 01:18:05.460
to live exactly as he lived.

886
01:18:05.460 --> 01:18:09.780
And it's only when she gets to a point where she cannot understand at all what's happening

887
01:18:09.780 --> 01:18:16.180
to her that he gives her another piece of that jigsaw puzzle, which is really amazing.

888
01:18:16.180 --> 01:18:23.500
So I want to give you Hebrews 1125 that the Lord ever lives to make intercession for us.

889
01:18:23.500 --> 01:18:31.660
Now one of the aspects of the Holy Eucharist that I think that Catholics are very poor on

890
01:18:31.660 --> 01:18:39.740
is the fact that Jesus is continuing his life and passion and death in the Holy Eucharist

891
01:18:39.740 --> 01:18:44.940
for us that it is a continuous sacrifice.

892
01:18:44.940 --> 01:18:53.140
So this is the final message of Volume 4, March the 18th, 1903.

893
01:18:53.140 --> 01:18:57.620
This morning as the Confessor asked me whether I felt the desire to suffer.

894
01:18:57.620 --> 01:19:03.820
I answered him, yes, but I felt more tranquil and enjoyed more peace and contentment when

895
01:19:03.820 --> 01:19:07.260
I wanted nothing but what God wants.

896
01:19:07.260 --> 01:19:12.580
Therefore I wanted to stop in the divine will.

897
01:19:12.580 --> 01:19:16.700
Then afterwards whom blessed Jesus came, he told me, my daughter, you have chosen the

898
01:19:16.700 --> 01:19:25.140
optimum because one who is always in my will binds me and binds me in such a way as to

899
01:19:25.140 --> 01:19:32.420
make a continuous power come out of me which keeps her in continuous attitude towards me.

900
01:19:32.420 --> 01:19:37.740
So much so that she forms my food and I hers.

901
01:19:37.740 --> 01:19:43.140
On the other hand, if the soul did great holy and good things and since it's not power that

902
01:19:43.140 --> 01:19:48.160
comes out of me, it cannot be an enjoyable food for me because I don't recognize it as

903
01:19:48.160 --> 01:19:51.220
my work of my will.

904
01:19:51.220 --> 01:20:00.060
So as long as we stay continuously surrendered in the divine will, then we please the Lord

905
01:20:00.060 --> 01:20:10.380
because it's his work and he continues his life, passion, death and resurrection in us.

906
01:20:10.380 --> 01:20:12.380
that's the end of volume 4.
